#X text 20 290 mlre - live cutting with cir~ (after mlr / mlre for norns);
#X text 20 330 TRACK ROW (left to right);
#X text 20 350 cells 0-15 : click = jump there and play. lit cell = playhead \, f 110;
#X text 20 370 play : start / stop (resumes where it stopped);
#X text 20 390 rec : record the input onto the track (overdub);
#X text 20 410 speed : octave selector -3 .. +3 (middle = 1x / each step doubles or halves) \, f 110;
#X text 20 430 semi : fine transpose in semitones -24..24 (added to speed);
#X text 20 450 rev : play backwards;
#X text 20 470 slew : seconds to glide when the speed changes (0 = jump);
#X text 20 490 lo / hi : loop only between these two cells (0-15);
#X text 20 510 len : clip length in seconds (max ~30). load sets it;
#X text 20 530 level : track volume;
#X text 20 550 pre : old audio kept when recording (1 = keep all / 0 = replace) \, f 110;
#X text 20 570 pan : left <-> right;
#X text 20 590 filter : 3 buttons = off / lowpass / highpass;
#X text 20 610 cutoff : filter frequency (26 Hz .. 20 kHz);
#X text 20 630 grp : 1-9 = tracks in the same group stop each other (0 = none) \, f 110;
#X text 20 650 load : open a sound file into the track;
#X text 20 670 clear : erase the tracks audio;
#X text 20 710 PATTERNS (P1-P4) record your cell clicks and loop them;
#X text 20 730 left button steps through: empty -> rec -> play -> stop -> play ... \, f 110;
#X text 20 750 right button: clear. the box shows the state;
#X text 20 790 MIXER   in = level of the inlets into all tracks / out = output volume / dsp = audio on/off \, f 110;
#X text 20 830 LFOs (L1-L6) move a track control up and down - you see the slider move \, f 110;
#X text 20 850 on : start / stop the LFO;
#X text 20 870 trk : which track (1-6);
#X text 20 890 target : v = level (volume) / p = pan / f = filter cutoff / o = pre (overdub) \, f 110;
#X text 20 910 shape : ~ sine / ^ triangle / / saw / n square / ? random (new value each cycle) \, f 110;
#X text 20 930 hz : speed in cycles per second;
#X text 20 950 center : middle point of the movement (0-1 of the controls range) \, f 110;
#X text 20 970 depth : how far it swings around the center (1 = full range);
#X text 20 1010 inlets: left + right audio in (mixed to mono) / outlets: left + right audio out \, f 110;
#X text 20 1030 all send names are local to this copy (prefixed with its own number) so several copies run side by side \, f 110;
#X obj 20 1070 inlet~;
#X obj 100 1070 inlet~;
